      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baddeck"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Baddeck derives from a Mi'kmaq place name meaning 'reversing flow' or 'place with island near'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baddeck"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alexander Graham Bell vacationed in Baddeck in 1885, where he built the Beinn Bhreagh laboratory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baddeck"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Alexander Graham Bell National Historic Site marks Bell's work, including the 1909 Silver Dart's first controlled powered flight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baddeck"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Grosvenor Hall, built in 1886, is a Romanesque Revival red sandstone building that once housed Baddeck's post office and custom house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baddeck"
    },
    {
